---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const BASE = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;

// Derek-Sivers /now convention: what I am focused on right now. Updated
// every quarter at most. Replace the whole list when the focus shifts —
// no archive.
const updated = '2026-05-17';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Now"
  description="What I am focused on right now — projects, writing, reading."
  lede={`Quarterly /now in the Sivers tradition. Last updated ${updated}.`}
  ogImage="now"
>
  <section class="prose">
    <h2>Building</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <a href="https://github.com/klarlabs-studio/nomi">Nomi</a> &mdash; local-first AI coding agent.
        Plan review before execution, capability-gated tools, BYO LLM. Tauri desktop + Go daemon.
        Your repo never leaves the laptop.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://github.com/felixgeelhaar/roady">Roady</a> &mdash; plan-of-record for AI coding
        agents. v0.12 shipped: nested sub-projects, live Kanban, cross-project board, drag-and-drop,
        SSE updates, auth gate.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://github.com/felixgeelhaar/tokenops">TokenOps</a> &mdash; local daemon
        measuring LLM spend, rate-limit headroom across Claude Max / ChatGPT / Copilot / Cursor,
        and output-side prompt patterns. v0.17.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://nox-hq.dev">Nox</a> &mdash; open-source security scanner with first-class
        AI app security (prompt injection, embedding leakage, agent over-privilege, MCP hardening,
        AIBOM). Apache 2.0, Go. v0.10.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href={`${BASE}armada`}>Armada</a> &mdash; campaign orchestration for Jira. Atlassian
        Marketplace, v4.2. Canonical site at <a href="https://armada.run">armada.run</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://github.com/klarlabs-studio/fortify">Fortify</a> &mdash; resilience patterns
        for Go services calling LLMs (circuit breaker, retry, rate limit, hedge, cost budget,
        stream timeout). v1.5.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://github.com/klarlabs-studio/bolt">Bolt</a> &mdash; zero-allocation
        slog.Handler for Go with first-class OpenTelemetry. genai add-on for OTel GenAI semconv.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://github.com/klarlabs-studio/statekit">Statekit</a> &mdash; typed statechart
        engine for Go. Backend workflows + AI agent runtimes on the same primitives.
      </li>
      <li>
        Cognitive stack &mdash;
        <a href="https://github.com/klarlabs-studio/mnemos">mnemos</a> (evidence + memory),
        <a href="https://github.com/felixgeelhaar/chronos">chronos</a> (time/pattern perception),
        <a href="https://github.com/felixgeelhaar/nous">nous</a> (commitment extraction),
        <a href="https://github.com/felixgeelhaar/praxis">praxis</a> (typed action layer),
        <a href="https://github.com/felixgeelhaar/olymp">olymp</a> (runtime / control plane).
        Domain-agnostic Go pieces an agent runtime composes.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://github.com/klarlabs-studio/mcp-go">mcp-go</a> &mdash; Go framework for
        building MCP servers. Used by most of the projects above.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Writing on</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>The plan-vs-evidence split in agent memory &mdash; why most "memory" features fix half the bug.</li>
      <li>The cost of skipping primitives in an agent runtime &mdash; what looks like a model problem usually isn't.</li>
      <li>Deploy / release / launch decoupling for teams shipping AI features.</li>
      <li>Field Notes essays land at <a href={`${BASE}writing`}>/writing</a>; subscribe in the footer.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Reading</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Team Topologies (re-read).</li>
      <li>The Goal (Goldratt) &mdash; flow-not-utilisation reframe.</li>
      <li>Click.</li>
      <li>Vibe Coding.</li>
      <li>Rethinking operating models.</li>
    </ul>

    <p class="muted">
      <em>Inspired by <a href="https://nownownow.com/about">nownownow.com</a>.</em>
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
